# Path-based season/team routing (e.g. /league2627/[team-slug]) was tried here
# and reverted -- Cloudflare's _redirects placeholders match any single path
# segment, so /:season and /:season/:team silently swallowed real static
# files that happen to have the same shape (/shared.js, /trades,
# /assets/hype.png), serving them as the homepage HTML instead of their real
# content. _redirects only applies to static assets, not Pages Functions, so
# /api/* was never affected -- but the client-side JS in shared.js broke
# (wrong MIME type), which is what broke the whole page.
#
# Revisit with a scheme that can't collide with real filenames (e.g. a
# distinguishing prefix like /s/:season) once something actually reads the
# season/team from the URL path -- right now nothing does, so there was no
# functional loss in removing this.
